  "womens-forum": {
    "title": "BLDEA's A S Patil College of Commerce Vijayapura",
    "url": "https://bldeaspcc.ac.in/womens-forum",
    "content": "Home Women’s Forum Women’s Forum Women Empowerment Cell A. S. Patil College of Commerce (Autonomous), Vijayapura has provided a platform to the women teaching/non-teaching staff along with girl students to express their views under the fundamental rights as prescribed in the Indian constitution. Thereby the girl students can come out with their problems related to the academic constraints and further familiar social-environmental difficulties they are facing. The addressed problems can be solved at the institution level respecting fully the social obligation on the part of the institution. If necessary financial assistance is also provided in deserving cases in terms of scholarships, free sheets and so on. Continuous care is taken by the institute/college till the stated problems by the girl students and the female staff (if any) till all the related problems are solved completely and the girl students can concentrate on their academic studies and further prospects. Matruchaya Under this head three members committee has been formed to look in to the problems of the girl students. It is commonly observed that female students are most of the time under certain mental pressures due to the circumstantial grounds wherein they are being brought up. As our aim states we should accommodate the students from the poor community, most of the students are deprived of healthy food containing vitamins, minerals, folic acid, iron etc. which are a must for their body building. The College here by provides the multi vitamins tablets, tonics, iron supplements, vitamins and minerals tablets to ensure proper hemoglobin at least at the basic standard levels. The girl students are provided with good quality sanitary napkins, machines for destroying the same etc. In such a way, female students of our college are nurtured and protected from any possible ailments under our banner MATRUCHAYA. Objectives A Women Empowerment committee is constituted having the following objectives: To accomplish a culture of respect for females and upgrade her self-esteem. To organize awareness programs in furtherance of the above lines. To conduct seminars, and workshops for women to get acquainted with the state policies issued under Directive Principles of the state. To motivate the young girls to be identified as “job givers” rather than “job seekers”. To educate women that empowered qualities shall avoid being at mercy in the male-dominated society To thrust on the fields like child marriage, dowry killings, female feticide etc. Any other harmful actions of the female gender shall tend to zero. Composition of Women Empowerment Cell for the A.Y. 2020-21 # Name of the Members Designation 1. Prof. B S Belagali, Principal of the College Chairman 2. Dr Bharati S Math Coordinator Faculty Representatives 2 Dr. Rashmi Patil, Co-ordinator, IQAC Member 3 Member 4 Prof. Laxmi Bagalkot, Assistant Controller of Examination Member 5 Dr. Ashwini A. Yarnal, Associate Professor, Member 6 Member 7 Prof. Bharati Nayakwadi, Assistant Professor, BCA Programme Member 8 Prof Veena More, Assistant Professor, BCA Programme Member Student Representatives 9 Member 10 Member 11 Member Courses Offered B.Com BBA BBM M.Com MBA PGDCA Apply Online Download Brochure Request a Call back Submit"
  },
