    "content": "Home Minority Cell Minority Cell Introduction Minority cell of the institution was established to empower the minority communities in the institution. This is a mechanism which offers assistance to minority students for their social and academic development. This also helps them to enroll for career orientation programs which would empower and equip them with the necessary skills for various career options. Institutions have been very keen to provide services to the educational and cultural needs of the Minority community along with other caste, creed and Nationality. The Minority Cell helps minority students including Muslims, Sikhs, Christians, Buddhists, Jain and Zorastrians (Parsis) etc. for their social & academic development. Objectives To accomplish a culture of respect for females and upgrade her self-esteem. To enhance equal opportunities for the education of minorities. To facilitate financial support to students from minority communities from governmental agencies and other sources. To create awareness among the minority students regarding various scholarship programs of State Government and UGC. To encourage enrolling for career orientation programs which would empower and equip them with the necessary skills to choose a career option. To ensure protection and reservation as provided in the constitution of India. The Minority Cell has been constituted to look into specific Responsibilities The Minority cell helps students belonging to a minority religion including Muslims, Sikhs, Christians, Buddhists, Jain and Zorastrians (Parsis) offers assistance to minority students for their social and academic development. And create awareness among minority students regarding various scholarship programs of the State Government and UGC. # Name of the Members Designation 1 Prof. B S Belagali, Principal Chairman 2 Co-ordinator 3 Faculty Representatives: Members Prof. V. S. Chikaraddi Prof. R. S. Chavan Prof. Mallikarjun G. M. 4 Students Representatives: Members Courses Offered B.Com BBA BBM M.Com MBA PGDCA Apply Online Download Brochure Request a Call back Submit"
